WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:02.104
Sedna, on its way in.

00:02.804 --> 00:12.853
It is falling towards its closest point, some time around 2076, and even that is seventy-six times the Earth's distance from the Sun.

00:13.303 --> 00:17.278
Then it climbs back out to nine hundred and thirty-seven times.

00:17.728 --> 00:27.273
No planet we know of could have put it on that path, and finding it in 2003 was part of what made astronomers ask what a planet is.
